f soft rose-gold and pearl white, filled with floating celestial musicians playing divine instruments and swarms of golden birds singing praises to Amitayus Buddha's name. The lighting is ethereal and warm, emanating from the Buddha himself as a primary light source that bathes the entire hall in a soft, diffused glow, creating gentle shadows and highlights across the jeweled surfaces. The composition balances symmetry with dynamic movement, using a wide perspective to capture both the grandeur of the architecture and the intimate expressions of the Bodhisattvas, while maintaining the sacred geometry described in the sutra. The overall palette consists of deep lapis lazuli blues, radiant golds, pearl whites, rose-gold highlights, and translucent crystal tones that shimmer with an inner luminosity.\n","qwen-llm-translate",true,"refresh",10,"Qwen3.8-9B-Q4_K_M.gguf",false,"refresh","mmproj-qwen3.5-9b-F16.gguf",false,"refresh",false,"medium",843682967233404,"randomize",8064,2,true,"cuda",32768,true,1536,"auto","auto"],"widgets_values_named":{"prompt":"The image is a wide cinematic illustration  of the Pure Land depicted as described in the Amitabha Sutra, rendered with intricate detail and spiritual reverence. The scene centers on Amitayus Buddha standing majestically on the right side of the frame, seated upon an eight-petalled lotus throne made of pure gold, his right hand raised in the gesture of reassurance (Abhaya mudra) and his left hand holding a jewel vase. He is surrounded by a magnificent assembly of Bodhisattvas who are listening attentively to his teachings. The setting is the Hall of Seven Treasures, an architectural marvel constructed from lapis lazuli, crystal, pearls, agate, red coral, and gold, with walls adorned with intricate carvings of celestial beings and scenes of enlightenment. Above the assembly floats a canopy of seven-colored light beams radiating from Amitayus Buddha's halo, while countless golden lotuses bloom in the air, each carrying Bodhi